WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:02.890
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:12.490
<b>November 10-12 
Culture Fair 
2-C Program</b>

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.860
All right, it's time for us to decide

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.480
what we'll do for the culture fair.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.830
<i>The culture fair, huh?</i>

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.940
<i>It's that time already?</i>

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.960
Committee member and secretary,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.080
go to the front.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:20.870
Right.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.290
And now...

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:30.950
You guys decide.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.750
<i>Come on, now, Chiaki...</i>

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.690
<b>Twentieth Haunting 
Under the Gilt</b>

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.600
Seriously?

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.590
Chiaki-chan must be tired!

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.780
My judo uniform...

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:28.410
Okay, so I'd like to decide what
we're doing for the culture fair.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:30.000
<b>November 10-12 
Culture Fair 
2-C Program</b>

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:29.990
Does anyone have ideas?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:33.910
What should we do?

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:37.510
<i>Maybe teachers are busy at this time of year.</i>

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.190
<i>Chiaki is also in charge of counseling.</i>

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.040
I heard that, this year, a lot fewer 
people are causing problems.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.910
Is that because of the work 
Chiaki's been doing?

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.210
I guess so.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:55.860
The first thing he did was to make friends 
with people likely to cause problems.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.030
I see.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.450
Even someone who's a little rough

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:05.440
wouldn't cause trouble for 
Chiaki, if they're friends.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.330
But he looks pale.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.220
H-Hey. Stop that.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.590
But he's so cute when he's sleeping!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.010
No phones allowed in school.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.930
He got mad at me.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.700
Jeez.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.520
Don't get cocky.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.900
You're lucky he didn't take your phone.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.860
I know that...

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.560
He's letting me get away with it, right?

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:47.360
Well, I'm lucky that Class 2-C has nothing 
but good students like you.

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.060
I can leave you alone, without worry.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.870
<i>He believes in us, doesn't he?</i>

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.410
<i>I have to live up to that.</i>

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:00.880
Hey, Tashiro!

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.070
Title:

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:06.550
"A Male High School Student Gazes 
Passionately at His Teacher."

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.470
It's so sad it isn't a female teacher!

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.490
Knock it off! I'll confiscate your phone!

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:15.780
Oh, no!

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.640
You two! Keep it down!

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:23.570
<i>In the end, 2-C settled on doing 
a demon-fighting game.</i>

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.490
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:30.200
And so, the English Conversation Club

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:33.660
<b>English Conversation Club 
Culture Fair Exhibit</b>

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.660
needs to decide what it's doing 
for the culture fair.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.910
The culture fair, huh?

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:37.160
You know,

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:41.620
people really liked the dubbing we 
did for the social, didn't they?

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.960
That's right.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.600
I was worried when we suddenly had 
Inaba-kun take over, though.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.520
No, I was more worried than anyone...

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:53.390
And that's what he says!

00:04:54.880 --> 00:05:00.070
Anyway, we want to do something even 
better for the culture festival, right?

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.120
Let's all come with an idea.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.310
Right!

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.470
I want to do English lessons for the kids!

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:13.250
<b>English Conversation Club 
Culture Fair Exhibit</b>

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.360
I want to call someone 
famous for an interview.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.910
Maybe something about stuff 
that happens in good movies?

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.060
Is something wrong, Inaba?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:45.650
No, I just realized we haven't 
seen Yamamoto since then.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.400
Konacchan, huh?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:52.700
She's annoying, but I am a little curious.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.080
Me, too.

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.410
Club President...

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.680
I sent her a bunch of messages,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.240
but she never responded.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.030
There's nothing else I can do.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:04.530
Yeah.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.480
And just like she said,

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:09.590
you can't force someone to attend.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.510
In the end, we just have 
to leave it up to her.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.150
<i>Up to her, huh?</i>

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:25.230
<b>English Conversation Club 
Culture Fair Exhibit</b>

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.480
I guess we haven't made our decision, huh?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.220
We'll decide next time, 
so think hard, everyone!

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.890
Okay!

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:32.160
Inaba, I got some information on Konacchan!

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.590
On Yamamoto?

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.270
Yeah.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:37.150
<i>Where do you get this stuff? Really!</i>

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:41.650
Before she came to JTB, she was at Jinmei.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:42.710
Jinmei?

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:48.380
<b>Jinmei High School</b>

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.430
Isn't Jinmei rather famous as a good school?

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:48.380
I guess she's pretty smart.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:52.270
But ever since she first showed 
up there, she acted weird.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.040
Weird?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.010
Uncooperative. Wanting to stand out.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.640
The type that's all about herself.

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:03.090
Who has to be the best at everything,

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.580
and always in charge.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:08.030
Why anime?

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.450
Why not a normal movie?

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.080
I see.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.790
<b>Jinmei High School</b>

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:23.450
Anyway, Konacchan would 
always show off her knowledge,

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.630
suddenly start yelling,

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:27.840
or answer out of turn in class...

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:32.130
All she ever did was try to 
draw attention to herself.

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:37.100
And her parents were called in, but...

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.460
Her classmates couldn't take it anymore,

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.440
and they started to ignore her.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.540
And so, she stopped going to school.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:03.670
And she transferred here?

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:09.090
At a business high school, an average 
class is easier to attend than at Jinmei.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.150
Her parents were trying 
to make it easy on her.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.760
Then maybe the problem's with the parents?

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.330
No, her family's supposedly pretty normal.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.500
Reputation with neighbors, their lifestyle,

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.350
how they act toward their kid...

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.690
It's all very normal.

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.410
<i>How do you have that information, too?</i>

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.130
<i>Do you have spies?</i>

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:30.610
The one thing

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.900
is that she has a big sister, 
five years older.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:34.780
A big sister?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.100
Her grades are always top of the class,

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.840
and she's really pretty.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:42.200
She's kind, and the picture
of an ideal student!

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:46.670
In other words, she has a complex 
toward her superior sister.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:47.760
Yeah.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.870
Looks like it started when she was little.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.510
And when she was little, she was very weak.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:59.020
Her family was really worried about her.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:04.650
<i>I finally understand the mystery 
behind Yamamoto's problems.</i>

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.460
<i>The old me was probably like that.</i>

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.300
<i>When I lived at my uncle's place,</i>

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.650
<i>Eriko was there, and she was 
two years older than I was.</i>

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.910
<i>Even though I wasn't their kid,</i>

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.060
<i>Uncle Hiroshi and Aunt Keiko 
never treated me differently.</i>

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.570
<i>But still...</i>

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:30.870
<i>I was sure there was a slight difference</i>

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.670
<i>between the way they treated me and Eriko.</i>

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:39.540
<i>But maybe I just imagined the whole thing.</i>

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.930
Good, huh?

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.020
What's so funny, Yushi-kun?

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.530
Oh, nothing!

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.340
I was just thinking that 
you always eat a lot.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:10.380
I'm still growing!

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:11.990
Right, Kuri?

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:15.330
That's true.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.390
Mom! Green peppers were in this again!

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.940
<i>I was always hungry in middle school, 
and Eriko hated all kinds of foods.</i>

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.110
<i>There was no way we'd eat the same food.</i>

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.030
<i>The problem was with me.</i>

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:33.100
<i>I convinced myself that they 
treated us differently,</i>

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:36.240
<i>so I made a huge deal out of 
things that were nothing.</i>

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:38.110
<b>The Seagull
Chekhov</b>

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.480
<i>Yamamoto may be making mountains</i>

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.580
<i>out of molehills, just like I used to.</i>

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:48.000
So maybe she's just gilding herself.

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.160
Gilding, huh?

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:12.350
<i>I won't lose to my sister. I won't!</i>

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.720
<i>Mom and Dad have just decided</i>

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:21.090
<i>that I'm the poor little sister, 
who can't do anything.</i>

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:25.030
<i>My sister's so free, but I...</i>

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.050
<i>I... I can...</i>

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.150
<i>It's all stupid!</i>

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:39.900
<i>I'm much better than all of these people!</i>

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.550
<i>Admit it!</i>

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:49.050
<i>Accept me... Accept me!</i>

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:06.810
So, master?

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:07.770
Fool?

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:09.770
What will you do?

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:10.740
About what?

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.420
About Yamamoto-sama.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:16.990
Tashiro-sama brought
you all that information...

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:19.330
Are you all right with leaving things alone?

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.670
Yeah...

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.960
Since she came to the club,

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:28.140
she may have wanted to interact with others.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:29.850
But...

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.810
Even if that's true,

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.980
unless she admits it,

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.360
there's nothing I can do.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.770
That is true, but...

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.570
Then butt out.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.090
<i>I want to do something, too.</i>

00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.450
<i>However,</i>

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:49.730
<i>it's arrogant to think that I 
can change someone's heart.</i>

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.620
<b>Faculty Office</b>

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.390
Excuse me.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:57.030
Don't read the manga you 
confiscate from students.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:59.130
Oh, Inaba...

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:04.130
<b>Oral Medicine

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.130
<b> Mangazine</b>

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:01.640
I see.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.140
You're on cleaning duty today?

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.220
<i>Medicine?</i>

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:06.540
Here.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:07.730
Thanks.

00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.620
Are things going well for the culture fair?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:13.990
Of course, you've got midterms first.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:15.480
Work hard at both.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.570
<i>Tch!</i>

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.200
<i>With us in charge, he totally has it easy.</i>

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:23.140
<i>I'm busy with the English 
Conversation Club, too.</i>

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.580
Listen, Chia—

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.030
Sir...

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.040
I want to talk to you.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.060
Good morning, Inaba-kun.

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:36.650
What? Is something bothering you?

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:38.300
If so, then let me—

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.200
What?!

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.410
A fight over what you're doing 
for the culture festival?

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.030
Where, Inaba?

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.580
Th-This way!

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.750
So, that's how it is.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.510
Oh, good morning...

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:55.510
I see.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.960
Aoki and this first-year named Yamamoto.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.950
Your club's got it rough...

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:04.160
Don't laugh at us.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:07.070
Well? Is there some good way to fix this?

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.360
Honestly, I don't know what to do.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:15.330
There's no silver bullet.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.780
Well, you'll just have to take your time.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.720
Is that all?

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.140
You don't have any better advice?

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:27.590
Did I tell you before about the guys 
in high school who were thugs,

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:30.390
but who changed their ways after graduation?

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:37.680
When that happens, nobody is focused
on what's going on around them.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:42.800
Whom you can see and when
all may be fated, from the start.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.490
In a case like this,

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:48.490
nothing anyone says matters.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:52.740
Whether someone recovers or 
not depends on their fate...

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:54.410
On their karma.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:56.000
Karma...

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:02.600
Of course, karma is something 
that you aren't sure exists

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.840
until you touch it.

00:15:10.120 --> 00:15:12.840
I need to hurry back.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.070
Hurry back to the classroom, too, Inaba.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:28.120
Oh, what a coincidence!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:32.070
Hey, Yamamoto, how have you been?

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.900
<i>Same as ever, huh?</i>

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:39.920
Can I sit here?

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.240
Actually,

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:48.910
the culture fair is in November, right?

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:53.040
The English Conversation Club 
has to do something.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:55.720
But we haven't yet decided what...

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.190
What do you think?

00:15:59.190 --> 00:16:01.310
Any good ideas?

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:05.120
<i>If she just comes to the club</i>

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:08.610
<i>and talks to everyone a little, maybe...</i>

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.940
Why?

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:15.780
Huh? Uh, well, that is...

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:19.700
Why should I think about something like that?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.130
Why?

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:25.890
In theory, you're part of the club, so...

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:27.450
In theory?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:33.800
Anyway, a club at that level 
has nothing to offer me.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.070
To offer you?

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.040
That's the only thing you have to say?

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:40.710
And don't just come up 
and talk to me, please.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.630
People will think I'm weird.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.640
Huh?

00:16:44.920 --> 00:16:46.230
Weird?

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:48.570
I just came to talk to you!

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:57.640
I really don't know how to 
deal with Yamamoto.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.390
Master!

00:17:00.150 --> 00:17:02.830
I just realized how helpless I am...

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.350
Cheer up, master!

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:08.170
We shall help you!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.590
You've got it nice and easy, huh?

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:14.970
And actually, if I could solve it with 
the <i>Petit</i>, I'd have no problems.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.840
Kuri-tan!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.250
How have you been, Kuri-tan?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.140
Oh, welcome back, Inaba.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.770
Kuri-tan!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.260
Someone else has it nice and easy.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:33.770
Sukiyaki!

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:35.940
Matsutake mushrooms! What a treat!

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.420
Great, huh?

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.470
Feels like a fall night...

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:41.380
That's right.

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:42.840
It's good.

00:17:42.840 --> 00:17:45.360
As long as I can drink, 
I don't care what it is.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:49.270
Or so you say, but you keep eating the meat!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:50.430
You caught me, huh?

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.130
It's so good!

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:54.970
Ruriko-san, you're the best!

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:00.380
You had good food on your trip, right?

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:01.810
This place is special.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.630
That's pretty fancy, though.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.830
A trip across Europe for your school trip.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:10.950
Exactly!

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:14.400
Next time, maybe I'll be a student?

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:18.900
This was my first trip to 
Neuschwanstein Castle,

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:22.330
and it's somewhere you should 
only go as part of a group.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:26.920
Listen to you talk.

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:30.410
Yeah, I know, I've never 
even been on a plane...

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:35.820
You should go overseas before you graduate.

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:38.650
For 30,000 yen, I can hook you up.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:39.670
For 30,000 yen?!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:42.590
How about three days and 
two nights in Singapore?

00:18:42.590 --> 00:18:43.850
It's pretty good!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.990
<i>A trip with Hase, huh?</i>

00:18:46.990 --> 00:18:48.520
<i>That sounds fun.</i>

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.660
What's this? A trip overseas?

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:53.740
Want me to take you somewhere fun?

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:54.810
No, thanks!

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:57.030
Aw, don't be like that.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.610
Your trips are more like wilderness survival!

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:02.230
I don't know about real-world adventures...

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.670
You're eating sukiyaki!

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.740
The meat's all gone.

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.390
You were a little too late.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:10.890
What a shame!

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.430
Sorry...

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:14.330
You guys!

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:16.550
Humans are so callous, chirp.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.360
Okay, bed time, chirp!

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.750
Goodnight, chirp!

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:23.170
Hmm... So that happened?

00:19:23.170 --> 00:19:26.840
Just be nice to this Yamamoto girl.

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:30.220
Give her credit for her interests in 
Russian literature and Truffaut.

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:32.510
Tell her she's a smart girl.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.260
Will that really work?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.860
Won't it make me like Aoki, 
only seeing one side to a person?

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:44.290
If there were just a good way to 
talk to her, it'd be easier...

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:48.410
But she never wants to talk to me at all.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.340
And I'm not great at talking 
to people, either.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:53.540
But...

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.870
The fact that Yamamoto came to 
the English Conversation Club,

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:01.260
and the fact that Aoki is 
our English teacher...

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.220
There must be some meaning.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.810
Some karmic connection they have to me.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:12.970
Why are you laughing?

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.710
That's so nice, a boy enjoying his youth!

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:16.430
Shut up!

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:19.360
Come to think of it!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.560
I didn't have a pillow 
fight on my school trip.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.990
Since we spent all our 
nights in luxury hotels.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.160
Don't humblebrag about that!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.160
It's the truth.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.080
I can't help it!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.040
This room is filled with a positive aura!

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:41.340
<i>If only I could really be open 
with Yamamoto, too.</i>

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.990
And so, for the culture festival...

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:49.180
<b>Culture Fair Exhibit 

00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:49.170
We'll be going a step further 
than our last dubbing,

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:52.600
to make our own English play!

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.600
<b>* Make an English Play</b>

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.770
Okay, we're gonna be busy!

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.940
<b>

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.940
Right!

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.870
This time, maybe we'll have you 
take the lead from the start.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:10.170
Hey! Heck, no!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.080
<b>English Conversation Club 
Proposal for School Fair Exhibit 

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.350
Oh, my? This aura...

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.230
What the hell was that?

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:28.620
Screw them all!

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:30.580
If I'd been there, it would've been...

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.100
They're all so stupid... So stupid!

00:21:35.360 --> 00:21:36.700
Stupid... Stupid.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.380
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.750
Sorry to keep you waiting, everyone!

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:15.640
It's finally time to make my appearance.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:17.260
What's going on here?

00:23:17.260 --> 00:23:20.430
Let us go beyond the horizon of adventure!

00:23:20.430 --> 00:23:23.250
Act now and get a free unicorn horn.

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:25.090
That sounds suspicious...

00:23:25.500 --> 00:23:27.920
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:29.380
<b>Twenty-first Haunting 
It Isn't a Manga!</b>

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:29.390
It Isn't a Manga!

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:33.180
At last, it is time to remove my eyepatch.

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:34.420
D-Don't tell me...

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:36.530
Antiquary!
